# Flask app settings
runtime/*

# Multi-Agent Investment Analysis System - .gitignore
CLAUDE*.md
# .claude/* excludes contents but NOT the .claude directory itself: git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so a bare `.claude` line
# would make the negations below silently do nothing.
.claude/*
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/rules/**
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
# The migration ledger stays IGNORED on purpose. It is keyed on line numbers of the
# root instruction file, which is itself never committed, so every row is unusable in
# a clone even where the destination it names is tracked. Operator-local by nature.
# "synced" is reserved for skills downloaded from the account. It is a cache, not
# source, and must never become committable even though skills/ is now tracked.
.claude/skills/synced/
.gemini
.gemini/*
GEMINI*.md
# Codex reads AGENTS.override.md before AGENTS.md. Overrides and historical variants
# remain local; only the repository-root contract is eligible for version control.
AGENTS*.md
!/AGENTS.md

# No project Codex configuration is shipped today. Keep accidental local settings out
# of version control; unignore individual portable files only after explicit review.
.codex/*

# Local things we ignore
# Operator-only notes. Nothing tracked may depend on anything in here.
docs/internal/
examples/~*
data_cache/
data_cache/*
# Keep only the directory
writing_samples/*
scratch/*

# Scratch dir should exist, but don't save anything there
scratch/*
!scratch/.gitkeep

# Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files

# Environment variables. DEFAULT-DENY: anything beginning `.env` is secret-bearing and
# only the tracked template is exempt. The previous enumeration (.env, .env-*, .env.old,
# .env.local, .env.*.local) left .env.production, .env.staging, .env.prod, .env.test,
# .env.backup, .env.save and .envrc committable -- a real leak vector for anyone whose
# deployment convention differs from the author's.
.env*
!.env.example

